// Module `clock`: waiting on a Clock's monotonic time (core.md, "Host"). Clock is a core
// capability type; a run's Clock comes from `main`'s granted parameters (CAP-4). Core has
// one waiting clock operation, `host.sleep_until`, on an absolute deadline in
// `host.mono_ns` nanoseconds; a relative wait is library code over it, here. Field
// legend: API.md. Nothing here admits anything (core.md, "Host").
/// Waits until `host.mono_ns(c)` has advanced by at least ns from its reading at entry:
/// one `host.mono_ns` reading plus ns is the deadline given to `host.sleep_until`, so it
/// returns at once when ns is 0 (WASI monotonic-clock subscribe-duration, Go time.Sleep).
/// A cancellation point at entry and while it waits (CONC-7); replay delivers the reading
/// and the completion without waiting (CAP-8).
/// Fails: Overflow (failure), before waiting, when the reading plus ns exceeds 2^64 - 1.
/// Ex: `std.clock.sleep_ns(c, 5_000_000)`
pub fn sleep_ns(c: Clock, ns: u64) waits {
    host.sleep_until(c, host.mono_ns(c) + ns)
}
